# 7. RESEARCH PAGE

This page should establish my research interests and showcase actual research work.

## Featured research

**Title:**

"Genomic Relatedness Alters Machine Learning Estimates of Carbapenem Resistance Prediction: Implications for African Genomic Surveillance."

Details:

- Conference: CPHIA 2026.
- Abstract ID: 2514.
- Status: Abstract accepted.
- Research area: Machine learning, antimicrobial resistance and genomic surveillance.
- Track: Primary Health Care, digital transformation and AI-enabled health systems.

The project investigates whether ignoring highly similar clonal genomes can inflate machine learning estimates of carbapenem resistance prediction performance.

The research uses synthetic gene presence/absence profiles rather than full genomic sequences.

Important methodological details include:

- 188 profiles from 53 founder clones.
- 75 near-identical descendants.
- A 0.95 Jaccard similarity threshold for detecting near-identical profiles.
- GroupKFold by clone to reduce leakage.
- SMOTE applied within training folds.

Verified cluster-aware AUC results:

| Model | AUC |
|---|---:|
| Logistic Regression | 0.846 |
| Linear SVM | 0.848 |
| Random Forest | 0.761 |
| XGBoost | 0.770 |

The naive overall AUC was 0.818.

These details should be used carefully and consistently with the final research poster or manuscript.

Clearly distinguish the research methodology, synthetic data and the conclusions. Do not imply that the study used a real-world clinical genomic dataset.

Include sections for:

- Research question.
- Background and motivation.
